{"parentUuid":"ec22366d-e692-4a9b-848a-99c8bc00c776","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01EkUsGzvdza2m7qZzxGmpu4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good — I now have the full pipeline. Here's what's actually happening.\n\n## Short answer\n\nA `.md` in `data_in/` **only** contains diagram‑to‑code (Mermaid) output if it was produced by the **vision enrich path** (`POST /api/vision/enrich`), and only for **PDF/DOCX/PPTX** sources. If your `uml-models (1).md` was itself a markdown *source* file, no vision ran on it at all — markdown/text inputs are passed straight through as a single text block. That's almost certainly why it \"wasn't obvious.\"\n\n## The two paths\n\n**1. Default ingest** (`core/extraction.py`) — figures are flattened/thrown away into plain markdown. No diagram-to-code. This is the untouched legacy path.\n\n**2. Vision path** (VIS-001, gated behind the `vision` ingest flag — [docmodel.py:14](prime-silo/runtime/benny/core/docmodel.py)) — two stages:\n- `build_docmodel` parses the doc into an element tree (per-element type/page/bbox), exports tables to JSON, and **saves a PNG crop per figure** — including vector/SVG architecture diagrams that have no raster image, via `cluster_drawings` region-cropping ([docmodel.py:462](prime-silo/runtime/benny/core/docmodel.py)).\n- `enrich_docmodel` runs the VLM ladder (qwen3vl reads the figure → qwen3-9b reviewer → validator → optional fidelity judge) and **stitches surrogates back in reading order**.\n\n## What the diagram-to-code actually looks like in the .md\n\nIn an enriched file, each figure becomes a fenced block with a provenance comment ([vision_pipeline.py:92](prime-silo/runtime/benny/core/vision_pipeline.py)):\n\n```\n<!-- docmodel id=<hash> type=picture page=3 figure_score=8 visual_score=7 -->\n```mermaid\nclassDiagram\n  ...\n```\n```\n\nTables become a markdown table + a ```json``` block; charts become ```json```; a figure the VLM couldn't render faithfully falls back to `*Figure (page): caption*`.\n\n**Key detail on your filename:** the enrich path sanitizes the stem (`_safe_stem`), so a real vision output would be named `uml-models__1_.md`, not `uml-models (1).md` with the space and parens. That strongly suggests your file is the **original source markdown**, not a vision-generated one — hence no Mermaid.\n\n## Where diagrams are stored (disk vs. RAG)\n\nNothing stores the *image pixels* in the knowledge graph. The layers:\n\n| Artifact | Location |\n|---|---|\n| Figure crop (PNG) | `<ws>/.benny/docmodel/crops/<stem>/<sha>.png` |\n| Full-page render (VLM grounding + fidelity judge) | `<ws>/.benny/docmodel/pages/<stem>/pN.png` |\n| DocModel (element tree, bbox, page) | `<ws>/.benny/docmodel/<stem>.json` |\n| Enriched markdown + provenance sidecar | `<ws>/.benny/docmodel/<stem>.enriched.md` / `.enriched.json` |\n| Copy fed to ingest | `<ws>/data_in/<stem>.md` ([vision_routes.py:106](prime-silo/runtime/benny/api/vision_routes.py)) |\n\nThen the **RAG/knowledge graph only ever sees the text** of that `data_in/*.md`. The Mermaid code / chart JSON / caption gets chunked, embedded into Chroma, and triple-extracted into Neo4j `Concept`/`Document` nodes **exactly like any other prose** — the diagram lives in the graph as its *textual surrogate*, not as an image. The pixels stay on disk in `.benny/docmodel/crops`, referenced only by the provenance comment (`id=... page=... bbox`).\n\n## To actually get diagram-to-code on a real doc\n\nPoint it at a **PDF** (not a .md) and run the vision path:\n\n```bash\n# stage the PDF, then:\nPOST /api/vision/docmodel?workspace=<ws>&source=uml-models.pdf\nPOST /api/vision/enrich?workspace=<ws>&source=uml-models.pdf&visual_judge=true\n```\n\nThen the `data_in/uml-models.md` it drops will have the ```mermaid``` blocks, and re-running RAG ingest will fold them into the graph.\n\nWant me to check a specific workspace to see whether a docmodel/enriched artifact exists for your uml-models file (which would tell us definitively which path it went through)?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":131,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11299,"cache_read_input_tokens":59424,"output_tokens":2892,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11299,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":131,"output_tokens":2892,"cache_read_input_tokens":59424,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11299,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11299},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CcawynY7ojes8snAeHNHR","type":"assistant","uuid":"0d7be345-6326-4629-994e-2014d349cd1d","timestamp":"2026-07-01T07:33:15.515Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16","sessionId":"31e0595d-3662-420b-b271-e67d95ee1eb2","version":"2.1.197","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
